WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:05.439
I'm going to be speaking with Tolia Lavan,
who is author of the book Culture War Lords

00:00:05.439 --> 00:00:08.840
My Journey into the Dark Web of White Supremacy.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.500
Tolia, great to have you on.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.250
I appreciate your time.

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:13.250
Thank you.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.330
I appreciate you having me on.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:22.220
So you did something very interesting, which
is you and Ben potentially harrowing, which

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:28.480
is you jumped into some of the dark recesses
of the Internet that I will often mention,

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.779
but recommend my audience not dove into.

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:37.140
And this includes white supremacy, anti-Semitism
and all sorts of different areas.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.890
Talk a little bit about why you did this and
sort of how you dipped your toes into this

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.019
pool to begin with.

00:00:44.019 --> 00:00:53.559
Yes, so I'm a Jewish woman and I've been writing
about the far right for a few years before

00:00:53.559 --> 00:00:55.430
the book even came out.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:01:02.719
And with that came a response from the white
supremacist white power community.

00:01:02.719 --> 00:01:09.680
And my reaction to various waves of harassment
that were vehemently misogynistic, vehemently

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.310
anti-Semitic was essentially to.

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:20.780
Instead of kind of curling up and shrinking
back and stop talking was to dove deeper,

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:25.439
I wanted to see who these people were, where
they were coming from, how they were getting

00:01:25.439 --> 00:01:26.579
to my Twitter feed.

00:01:26.579 --> 00:01:33.009
And, you know, it was sort of a situation
where the abyss was looking at me and I decided

00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:38.860
to gaze back and drag what I saw back out
into the light.

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:44.590
So what did you find about the source of many
of the the sort of hateful and trolling messages

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:47.140
that you were getting?

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:52.579
So I decided to take a broad view and look
at both.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:59.010
The development of the contemporary white
power movement and what it looks like, how

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:05.920
it manifests and where they congregate, so
I spent a lot of time looking at particularly

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:15.470
an encrypted chat app called Telegram and
which has like very strong free speech protections

00:02:15.470 --> 00:02:19.170
and sort of never bandz content, really.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:25.080
So it's become kind of a thriving ground for
white supremacists to particularly in twenty

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:31.470
nineteen, faced some Banning's from mainstream
social media like Facebook and Twitter.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:36.970
And so that's where I spent a lot of my book
research looking into.

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:43.130
And I found a lot of different tendencies
in communities of interest within the white

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:47.970
power movement that I spend the book, Culture
Warlords Exploring.

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:52.230
Did you talk a little bit about how you existed
in some of these spaces?

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:57.030
I mean, did you develop a character or a series
of characters, alter egos that that you kind

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.540
of took on?

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:04.930
Yeah, so I didn't actually set out to write
a gonzo journalism book, it's just that when

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:11.500
you're a Jewish woman and when you've been
kind of an outspoken antifascist for years,

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.400
it's hard to get in the front door.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.180
People who are white supremacists won't get
you an interview.

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:18.520
You know, I am.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:23.010
One of my earlier attempts was to try and
get into.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:27.270
There's a sort of.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:37.060
Powerlifting based white supremacist pagan
cult that that has these solstice celebrations

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:42.510
and I tried to get in just as a reporter and
much later one of the guys I was talking to

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:45.530
was like, oh, we would never let a Jew in
anyway.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:53.110
So, you know, it was hard to get in the front
door, but and so as a result, I found myself

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:57.920
sort of having to get a little creative and
find these back door roots.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:05.570
And that included making sock puppets, sock
puppet accounts to just kind of squat and

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:11.010
listen and in some other cases, having to
be a little more proactive and inventing kind

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:16.760
of identities from whole cloth in order to
get into more private chats.

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:28.630
And in one case, I infiltrated a white supremacist
dating site, white dot net, with the whole

00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:36.510
character who didn't look like me or have
my background as kind of a course Brooklyn

00:04:36.510 --> 00:04:37.760
Jew.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:44.720
And I got these forlorn white supremacists
looking for love to write love letters to

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.354
their ideal white wife and send them to me.

00:04:47.354 --> 00:04:52.870
And I printed them in the book and it was
sort of a car crash between Nicholas Sparks

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:55.210
and Mein Kampf.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:05:00.480
Did you make any of what you would consider
to be friends during this process?

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:08.910
No, I mean, it's not generally my.

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:15.510
My practice to make friends with people who
want me dead, right, but within my character,

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.750
I mean, I had.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:22.780
I was I tried not to be that active and infiltrator,
you know what I mean?

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:26.000
You don't want to be the one amping up the
stochastic terror.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:31.801
You want to say just enough to pass and remain
in the room.

00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:35.860
But in one particular event, there was sort
of a.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:41.210
And may fight being organized between pagan
white supremacists and Christian white supremacists

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:47.020
to support the presidential run of a white
nationalist Satanist.

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:52.580
And so I got deeply involved in the planning
chat's for that group and wound up talking

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:59.760
pretty extensively to one Christian extremist
and telling him all about how his fascist

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:03.310
love of Christ had saved my life.

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:08.660
Just funny things to have to do from my apartment
in Brooklyn as far as I'm interested in this

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:10.040
religious component.

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:13.810
In your experience kind of weaving your way
through these communities, you know, we know

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:19.240
about the Christian roots of the KKK as an
example, but at the same time, there are many

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:23.930
people who get pulled into white nationalism
and white supremacy who are not particularly

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:24.930
religious.

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:28.460
How relevant was religion, would you say,
in these different enclaves?

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:35.050
Well, the group that I was studying primarily
were sort of these radicalized white power

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:36.090
guys, right?

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:43.980
We know that within the mainline sort of MAGGA
movement, which has its fascistic undertones,

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:46.330
religion plays quite a large role.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:51.110
This idea that Trump is selected by God and
we must fight for him and everyone else is

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:52.110
of Satan.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:56.180
The group that I was speaking to tended to
skew younger.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:07:02.420
We're a little more disaffected with religion,
but what they really took from religion in

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:08.540
the case of the Christian white supremacists,
there was this absolute fixation on the Crusades

00:07:08.540 --> 00:07:14.980
as kind of a lost cause, this battle between
noble white warriors and swarthy interlopers

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:22.699
that they kind of interposed onto contemporary
anti-immigrant anti-Muslim dialog.

00:07:22.699 --> 00:07:28.960
So it was kind of like them viewing themselves
as crusaders and flying the Templar Crossette

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.560
racist realities.

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:36.880
In the case of pagan white supremacists, heathen
white supremacists, you have this fixation

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:45.180
on Vikings, this idea of white manliness,
and the idea of the Norse pantheon as an indigenous,

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:46.260
white European religion.

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:49.090
And one of the things that sort of.

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:56.479
Surprised and tickled me was that many heathen
white supremacists are drawn to the worship

00:07:56.479 --> 00:08:05.740
of the Norse pantheon by the idea that Christianity
was started by a Jew and is thus tainted by

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:07.520
the Jewish taint forever.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:10.800
And so you can literally be Jesus Christ.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:16.540
And that's not enough for some anti-Semite,
which was sort of a funny discovery to make

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:19.300
via the people you came across.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:20.621
What portion did you get this?

00:08:20.621 --> 00:08:22.800
I mean, this is it could be just difficult
to tell.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:28.860
But did you get a sense of what portion would
be willing to sort of go and actually take

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:32.539
violence into their own hands in the real
world versus how many of them are sort of

00:08:32.539 --> 00:08:34.349
existing in these online spaces?

00:08:34.349 --> 00:08:37.529
And that's as far as they're willing to go.

00:08:37.529 --> 00:08:42.209
So when I tallied up the telegram groups I
was involved in and of course that's not the

00:08:42.209 --> 00:08:47.529
most scientific measure, but I joined between
ninety and a hundred of these chats and collectively

00:08:47.529 --> 00:08:50.670
they had tens of thousands of members.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:51.670
Sure.

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:57.990
And one of the big problems facing researchers
and journalists in this area is that it's

00:08:57.990 --> 00:09:05.240
quite simply very hard to tell which young
man spewing violent and genocidal rhetoric

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:07.389
is going to be the one that snaps.

00:09:07.389 --> 00:09:13.069
So, you know, I have a close friend who is
an anti fascist and who was several times

00:09:13.069 --> 00:09:21.420
threatened directly by Robert Bowers, who
went on to allegedly shoot 11 Jews in the

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:22.870
Tree of Life synagogue.

00:09:22.870 --> 00:09:25.199
And it's just very hard to tell.

00:09:25.199 --> 00:09:31.279
It's hard to tell when you're looking at the
sea of essentially stochastic terror, this

00:09:31.279 --> 00:09:36.629
sort of perpetual motion machine towards radicalization
and violence.

00:09:36.629 --> 00:09:38.250
Who is going to be the one to snap?

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:43.709
And that's why I talk about how the importance
isn't necessarily the raw numbers.

00:09:43.709 --> 00:09:49.089
Yeah, but about the tenor of the conversation.

00:09:49.089 --> 00:09:55.019
And when you are marinating in stochastic
terror, marinating in racial violence, marinating

00:09:55.019 --> 00:10:00.459
in the dehumanization of your supposed racial
enemies, you know, this is an environment

00:10:00.459 --> 00:10:07.070
that's specifically queued to get people to
snap, to radicalize, to engage in violence,

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:09.329
to stockpile guns.

00:10:09.329 --> 00:10:16.970
When I have interviewed former white nationalist
and white supremacists, including folk, folks

00:10:16.970 --> 00:10:22.889
like Frank Menck and many others of these
folks who have now become anti-racist advocates,

00:10:22.889 --> 00:10:27.999
they almost UNILAG almost unanimously tell
the same story about how they were pulled

00:10:27.999 --> 00:10:36.050
in, which is that they sort of found either
an attention or what they felt as support

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:40.319
or a community where they had an absence of
it.

00:10:40.319 --> 00:10:44.769
Typically in their family life growing up
like that's it's almost cliche, but it's the

00:10:44.769 --> 00:10:47.410
story they almost all tell.

00:10:47.410 --> 00:10:52.680
Did you get any sense of at the individual
level how the folks you came across ended

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:54.220
up in these movements?

00:10:54.220 --> 00:11:00.709
Yeah, I mean, particularly on the white supremacist
dating site, there was often kind of a there

00:11:00.709 --> 00:11:06.670
was a segment, you know, in the BIOS where
people describe their politics and how they

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:08.790
came to be on a white supremacist dating site.

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:11.399
And a lot of the story started with YouTube.

00:11:11.399 --> 00:11:16.160
There were a lot of divorces in their back
stories.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:21.620
You know, there were a lot of people in the
military, you know.

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:24.569
I would say that the most.

00:11:24.569 --> 00:11:27.329
Consistent theme was a sense of alienation.

00:11:27.329 --> 00:11:33.949
Right, and I think, as we all know, that that
sense of alienation, lack of community, desire

00:11:33.949 --> 00:11:40.899
for purpose, it crosses socioeconomic lines,
it crosses geographical divides.

00:11:40.899 --> 00:11:46.720
You know, it's really a question of sort of
how deep is your feeling of alienation and

00:11:46.720 --> 00:11:47.720
displacement?

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:50.160
And that can have a lot of different causes.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:55.300
I think it's a mistake when people say, oh,
it's just toothless.

00:11:55.300 --> 00:12:02.569
Cleatus in his mother's basement, when what
I saw was really a movement that spanned geographical

00:12:02.569 --> 00:12:10.709
lines, socioeconomic lines is where people
with lives and sometimes spouses, sometimes

00:12:10.709 --> 00:12:12.129
people who are in college.

00:12:12.129 --> 00:12:19.869
You know, the myth that everyone is sort of
southern and uneducated is really a self absorbing

00:12:19.869 --> 00:12:23.860
myth that white liberals used to say it couldn't
be anyone in my neighborhood, couldn't be

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:27.810
anyone in my school or my acoa, when in fact
it could.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:29.889
It's just a matter of people feeling lost.

00:12:29.889 --> 00:12:36.769
And the white supremacist white power movement
really offering you this mythos of you can

00:12:36.769 --> 00:12:40.250
become involved, you can save the white race.

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:43.839
We will give you a sense of purpose in your
life.

00:12:43.839 --> 00:12:46.239
And I think a lot of us are looking for a
sense of purpose.

00:12:46.239 --> 00:12:52.670
A lot of us are feeling lost and alienated
and we all find that in different ways.

00:12:52.670 --> 00:12:57.749
But that's the sort of compelling argument
they make, as is here's a chance to be part

00:12:57.749 --> 00:13:00.320
of a community of people saving the white
race.

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:05.110
Yeah, what's interesting about that is, you
know, there's a similar pattern to a lot of

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:10.410
the people that get sucked into the cult of
Trump ism, which is believing that it will

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:17.550
provide solutions to problems that may well
be real, but but they get tricked about where

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:18.870
the solutions are.

00:13:18.870 --> 00:13:23.689
And that seems to be kind of interesting overlap
in hearing hearing you describe it.

00:13:23.689 --> 00:13:29.959
Yeah, I mean, I think that's true of any sort
of radicalizing movement, right?

00:13:29.959 --> 00:13:30.959
Yeah.

00:13:30.959 --> 00:13:38.570
Is that they look at you, look at your vulnerabilities,
look at what you're seeking and then become

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:42.019
that, you know, love bomb you.

00:13:42.019 --> 00:13:49.100
Although, frankly, the tenor of conversation
is quite puerile and often very cruel.

00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:54.449
There's not a lot of love bombing going on,
but there is a sense of like you are a warrior,

00:13:54.449 --> 00:14:00.999
you know, there's really a regression and
to very toxic and narrow gender roles.

00:14:00.999 --> 00:14:09.600
This this idea of kind of you will be a manly
man, a warrior for the white race and encouragement

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:12.399
towards survivalism, towards stocking up guns.

00:14:12.399 --> 00:14:20.029
But really the sense of kind of propping up
embattled masculinity and making that be part

00:14:20.029 --> 00:14:29.160
of a community that has this sort of overall,
quote unquote, noble purpose.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:35.509
The book is fascinating, its culture war Lords,
My Journey into the Dark Web of White Supremacy.

00:14:35.509 --> 00:14:38.259
We've been speaking with the book's author,
Tolia Laventhol.

00:14:38.259 --> 00:14:41.129
I so appreciate your time today.

00:14:41.129 --> 00:14:42.160
Thank you so much.

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:46.899
Yeah, and the book is available on Amazon
at your local indie store, which you should

00:14:46.899 --> 00:14:53.089
please support during the pandemic and everywhere
books are sold and it goes into great detail

00:14:53.089 --> 00:14:56.569
about not just contemporary privacy, but The
David Pakman Show at David Pakman Dotcom.

